{"term":"tariff","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1c39aa772464352985","definition":"A system of government-imposed duties levied on imported or exported goods; a list of such duties, or the duties themselves.","example":"This question may be placed in another light. It is agreed on all sides, that numbers are the best scale of wealth and taxation, as they are the only proper scale of representation. Would the convention have been impartial or consistent, if they had rejected the slaves from the list of inhabitants, when the shares of representation were to be calculated, and inserted them on the lists when the tariff of contributions was to be adjusted?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antitariff","countertariff","non-tariff","nontariff","posttariff","pretariff","punitive tariff","retaliatory tariff","social tariff","tariff barrier","tariffication","tariffism","tariffist","tariffite","tariffize","tariffless","whole life tariff"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tariff#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d5acce3952f2b27a06","definition":"A schedule of rates, fees or prices.","example":"Under a peak/off-peak electricity tariff, you pay a lower rate for the power when demand is less.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["plan"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antitariff","countertariff","non-tariff","nontariff","posttariff","pretariff","punitive tariff","retaliatory tariff","social tariff","tariff barrier","tariffication","tariffism","tariffist","tariffite","tariffize","tariffless","whole life tariff"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tariff#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bb322785b66d1bf7ba","definition":"A sentence determined according to a scale o